  "summary": "Only four supplied documents directly apply multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling to early prediction of septic deterioration: [V0019], [V0018], [V0017], and [V0020]. Their reported datasets and metrics are heterogeneous and not strictly comparable: LedgerGuard accuracy 0.83 [V0019]; AgriSat-4 F1 0.76 [V0018]; Atlas-ICU AUROC 0.69 [V0017]; and CellLife MAE 0.90 [V0020], with MAE being an error metric rather than a discrimination score. Prior-work mentions of the sepsis partial-pooling line in studies of other problems, such as [V0177] and [V0111], were not treated as applications. Because exactly five IDs were requested, [V0009] is appended only as a format-filling non-match: it addresses early prediction of septic deterioration on Atlas-ICU with accuracy 0.82 but uses decentralised training without pooled records, not the requested Bayesian hierarchical partial-pooling method.",
